  "tagline": "Distributed SQL database built on Lucene for real-time analytics over machine, IoT and JSON data.",
  "description": "CrateDB is a distributed SQL engine that reuses Lucene and Elasticsearch-derived clustering, so every column is indexed by default and tables shard and replicate automatically. It speaks the PostgreSQL wire protocol, handles nested objects and arrays natively, and adds full-text, geospatial and vector search, which suits industrial IoT, fleet telemetry and log-like data that needs ad-hoc aggregation. Crate.io sells CrateDB Cloud and enterprise support, while the database itself is Apache-2.0. It is not a transactional database: there are no multi-statement transactions, and new writes become visible to queries after a refresh interval.",
